  "input_and_result_semantics": [
    "An explicit project_saved_dfg operation on the existing graph alignment route accepts full supplied DfgAlignmentLogResult state and calls only native supplied-result projection overloads; alignment search and score recalculation do not run.",
    "Original CSV/XES, complete typed EventTable and byte-safe raw EventLog sources are supported with exact native selectors. Complete DFG JSON or text models retain explicit start/end boundaries including empty maps.",
    "Native result, workbench and report envelopes are selected explicitly. Saved results are supplied as an actual original multipart File or inline text with presence conflicts rejected. Complete original upload bytes and outer envelopes stay inspectable.",
    "All native moves, computed flags, finite and nonfinite scores, unique variants and search counters are retained. NativeString carriers preserve arbitrary byte and WTF8 labels; unsigned counters accept exact tokens or decimal strings.",
    "Canonical supplied state, source/model snapshots, native metrics, byte-safe raw projected log and optional legacy log/XES/model exports are independently retained. A failed projection or export does not discard the submitted result.",
    "The same original source/model File objects can be reused from a completed grouped-log DFG alignment with the whole captured workbench as an actual saved File. Explicit inline editing replaces that File input.",
    "A source-bound direct native witness verifies different supplied routes for identical traces change projected timestamps and adjacent-pair metrics. Supplied content does not establish authenticity, provenance or optimality.",
    "Existing alignment and projection algorithms are unchanged. Tests and HTTP proofs establish this input/result workflow; they do not establish full reference equivalence."
  ],
